# The certify and checks environments: the package's runtime deps (pyproject.toml [project] dependencies)
# plus the test and lint tools. torch comes as the CPU build from the PyTorch index, which is made uv's
# primary index at compile time (see the command in the .txt header): that index rehosts common packages
# (markupsafe, jinja2, ...) as byte-different files, so it must be primary for the recorded hashes to match
# the files a --require-hashes pip install actually fetches from it. Everything the index does not host
# resolves from PyPI (the extra index). The index URLs are emitted into the lock, so no --extra-index-url
# is needed at install time.
